      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mikewest/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Thanks @bzbarsky.\r\n\r\nI think the major outstanding question is whether the current approach of reusing the existing attribute modification tools is workable. Mutation events seem safe, given that they're triggered asynchronously. `DOMNodeInsertedIntoDocument` seems safe, as it won't trigger again upon attribute modification. `DOMAttrModified` is a problem, as you note. I'm pretty sure Chrome doesn't support it, but browsers that do would be sad.\r\n\r\nWould it be better to just reach into the guts of the attribute node and change its value, bypassing these events entirely?",
    "state": "COMMENTED",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/2373#pullrequestreview-39962799",
    "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/pulls/2373",
